  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To find the percentage of sales from sunflower bouquets:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Faraday owns a flower shop.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "No problem—the type of business doesn’t change the calculation.\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12\\text{ sunflower bouquets}}{50\\text{ total bouquets}}\\times 100\\%=24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many sunflower bouquets did Faraday sell per day on average during that week? Additionally, Faraday's flower shop was open for 6 days during that week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets over 6 days. The average per day was:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{6}=2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ sunflower bouquets per day}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $3 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Noted: individual sunflowers cost **$3 each**. To calculate the revenue from individual sunflowers, we would also need to know how many individual sunflowers Faraday sold.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day from individual sunflowers and $56 per day from bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over three days:\n\n1. **Individual sunflowers:**\n\n\\[\n\\$26 \\times 3=\\$78\n\\]\n\nAt \\$3 each:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$78}{\\$3}=26\n\\]\n\nSo, Faraday sold **26 individual sunflowers**.\n\n2. **Sunflower bouquets:**\n\n\\[\n\\$56 \\times 3=\\$168\n\\]\n\nAt \\$8 per bouquet:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$168}{\\$8}=21\n\\]\n\nSo, Faraday sold **21 bouquets**.\n\nThe exact total number of sunflowers cannot be determined unless we know how many sunflowers are in each bouquet. Thus, the known results are:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26\\text{ individual sunflowers and }21\\text{ bouquets}}\n\\]\n\n(Note: this new information conflicts with the earlier figure of 12 bouquets sold during the week.)",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over three days:\n\n- Individual sunflowers:  \n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$26\\times 3}{\\$3}=26\n  \\]\n\n- Bouquets sold:  \n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$56\\times 3}{\\$8}=21\n  \\]\n\n- Sunflowers in those bouquets:  \n  \\[\n  21\\times 12=252\n  \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of sunflowers sold was:\n\n\\[\n26+252=\\boxed{278\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With individual sunflowers priced at **$2 each**:\n\n- Individual sunflower revenue over 3 days:\n  \\[\n  26\\times 3=\\$78\n  \\]\n\n- Individual sunflowers sold:\n  \\[\n  78\\div 2=39\n  \\]\n\n- Bouquets sold over 3 days:\n  \\[\n  (56\\div 8)\\times 3=21\n  \\]\n\n- Sunflowers in bouquets:\n  \\[\n  21\\times 12=252\n  \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of sunflowers sold was:\n\n\\[\n39+252=\\boxed{291\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
